                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Super short, isometric puzzle game where you use the arrow keys to move an angular character over tiles to pick up gems, unlock an exit, then reach it.\n\nPuzzles are largely straightforward, save for maybe a couple of curve balls with regards to backtracking, but are still satisfying enough to make each screen's worth of content feel worthwhile and devoid of filler. There's really little more to be said other than for the soothing piano score and clean, minimalist visuals that comprise the fifteen minutes or so it takes to get to the end.\n\nA pleasant apéritif between games, Flightless is a free game easily worth investing some of your free time into.",
